  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930198",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-112383",
      "knowledge_point_id": "c7df31c9-b27a-5ce2-93c8-178ba96da000",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining a Rate of Change",
      "problem": "After charging the battery of a PC, the percentage of charge decreases at a rate of $c(t)=100\\cdot {5}^{-0.2t}$ percent per hour, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since the battery had completed its charge. What will be the rate of decrease after $5$ hours?",
      "worked_solution": "Since we want to determine the rate of decrease in the amount of charge after $5$ hours, we have $t=5.$\n\nThus, the rate of decrease of the amount of charge after $5$ hours will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c(5) & =100\\cdot {5}^{-0.2(5)} \\\\  & =100\\cdot {5}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{100}{5} \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of decrease will be $20$ percent per hour.",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$4$ percent per hour",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$40$ percent per hour",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$10$ percent per hour",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$2$ percent per hour",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$20$ percent per hour",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "easy",
