  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930198",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-48914",
      "knowledge_point_id": "c7df31c9-b27a-5ce2-93c8-178ba96da000",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining a Rate of Change",
      "problem": "The birth rate of a herd of elephants in a region in Africa is modeled by the function  $B(t)=500\\cdot {2}^{0.125t}$ while the rate of death is modeled by $D(t)=400\\cdot {3}^{0.125t}.$ In both cases, $t$ represents the number of years since $1990.$  \n\nWhat was the rate of change of the elephant population in that region in $1998?$",
      "worked_solution": "The  rate of change in the number of elephants  $t$ years since $1990$ is equal to the difference between the two given rates, that is\n\n$$\nB(t)-D(t).\n$$\n\nAs $1998$ is $8$ years after $1990$, we have $t=8.$  Hence, the  rate of change in the elephant population in that region in $1998$ was \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(8)-D(8) & =500\\cdot {2}^{0.125(8)}-400\\cdot {3}^{0.125(8)} \\\\  & =500\\cdot 2-400\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-200.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the elephant population was $-200$ elephants per year.",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$-94$ elephants per year",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$-220$ elephants per year",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$-200$ elephants per year",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$420$ elephants per year",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$240$ elephants per year",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "moderate",
      "provenance": {
