  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930198",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-72004",
      "knowledge_point_id": "fa38f112-466c-50e9-ac08-be72b6f53782",
      "knowledge_point": "Relating a Derivative to a Rate of Change",
      "problem": "Jason, a biologist, is measuring the growth of bacteria in a Petri dish by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in hours, since he started his observations:\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of bacteria in the dish.\n\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the number of bacteria in the dish is increasing.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $N(t)$ and $r(t)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The function $N(t)$ gives the number of bacteria inside the dish after $t$ hours. Then,\n\n$$\n{N}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}N(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }N}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${N}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of bacteria is increasing at time $t$, which is the same as $r(t).$ Therefore, the relationship between $N(t)$ and $r(t)$ is ${N}^{′}(t)=r(t).$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{N}^{′}(t)=r(t)",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{N}^{′}(t)=-r(t)",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "N(t)=-{r}^{′}(t)",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "N(t)={r}^{′}(t)",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "N(t)=r(t)",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-72004",
        "kp_title": "Relating a Derivative to a Rate of Change",
        "kp_href": null
      },
      "topic_id": 296,
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930198/state.json",
