  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930500",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-62256",
      "knowledge_point_id": "947eb2bb-0443-5740-9d45-847c70877270",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given Some Lengths",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930500/assets/54212c293853632fd46716b6216a74c3579bf89349e8b2c5cefafe80e40e42cf.png)\n\nAssuming that all side faces have the same height of $9\\,\\text{m}$, find the total surface area of the square pyramid above using its net.",
      "worked_solution": "The net of our pyramid is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930500/assets/09eff98ca31b4bb350e2d793dcfa6e6972de25bb3b613c898533068c36fe9a78.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the base of the pyramid is a square with a side equal to $2\\,\\text{m}.$ Hence:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=2\\times 2=4\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEach side face of our solid is triangle, where the base is $2\\,\\text{m}$ and the height is $9\\,\\text{m}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the triangle}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times 2\\times 9=9\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the pyramid consists of $1$ square (base) and $4$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =(\\text{Area of the square})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the triangle}) \\\\  & =4+4\\times 9 \\\\  & =4+36 \\\\  & =40\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "9\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "40\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "36\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "4\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "46\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
