  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930904",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-99275",
      "knowledge_point_id": "4974097a-95c9-5835-ba1d-46480efab66b",
      "knowledge_point": "Computing the Limit at Infinity of a Power Function With an Even Power",
      "problem": "Find ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(8{x}^{12}).$",
      "worked_solution": "The graph $y={x}^{12}$ looks similar to an upward parabola, so\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{x}^{12}=\\infty .\n$$\n\nMultiplication by the positive constant $8$ does not affect the limit at infinity. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(8{x}^{12})={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }({x}^{12})=\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
